+# HR corridors clamped to watch zones
+
+## Change
+`gen.py` `hr_target()` now emits `{"units": "%lthr", "start": lo, "end": hi}` instead of `{"units": "%lthr", "value": lo, "end": hi}`.
+
+## Why
+The readback (`readback/event-184233-as-sent.json`) shows we sent `value`/`end`. The API accepted it (steps populated), so the problem was not rejection. Per the colleague's note, the key name for the lower bound selects the FIT export mode. `value`+`end` becomes a zone-mapped Lap-HR target, which the watch clamps to its own zones. `start`+`end` becomes an Instant-HR corridor, which shows the raw bpm Intervals computes (% x Intervals LTHR 172). That matches the watch-notes symptoms: every step showed a watch zone band, and changing the watch LTHR moved the bands but they stayed zone edges.
+
+## Colleague's note: what applied
+- Applied: `value` -> `start`, keeping `%lthr` units. This is the only change.
+- Already consistent: we use percentages, not bpm. `units: "bpm"` and `start_bpm`/`end_bpm` were already ruled out in watch-notes.
+- Not applied: the top-level `description` text grammar. Our readback shows `workout_doc.steps` populated and the notes don't report a web-UI problem. I left it alone.
+
+## Not verified
+I couldn't push or sync a watch, so the expected watch result is untested: 68-75 -> ~117-129 bpm, 88-93 -> 151-160, 75-82 -> 129-141, 65-72 -> 112-124. Please push a test event, read it back and check the watch. Also confirm that the readback shows `start`, since the API could normalise it.
